<p class="lt-chem-36401">Acid chlorides react with alcohol nucleophiles to produce esters. This reaction is the preferred method for preparing esters. Pryidine is often added to the reaction mixture to remove the HCl produced.</p>

<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Organic_Chemistry/Organic_Chemistry_(Morsch_et_al.)/21:_Carboxylic_Acid_Derivatives-_Nucleophilic_Acyl_Substitution_Reactions/21.04:_Chemistry_of_Acid_Halides" class="mt-section" id="section_12"><span id="General_Reaction_2"></span><h4 class="lt-chem-36401 editable">General Reaction</h4>

